"sections": [
{
"title": "Prep",
"steps": [
{
"text": "<b>Soften the cream cheese.</b> Cut it into 1-inch cubes and leave it on the counter while you cook (or microwave 15–20 seconds)."
},
{
"text": "<b>Prep the vegetables.</b> Cube the potatoes, dice the onion, and mince the garlic."
}
]
},
{
"title": "Cook",
"steps": [
{
"text": "<b>Heat the broth.</b> Bring it to a gentle simmer in a large stock pot over medium-high heat."
},
{
"text": "<b>Add everything else.</b> Stir in the potatoes, onion, garlic, seasoned salt, and bacon grease, if using."
},
{
"text": "<b>Simmer.</b> Cook on medium about 15 minutes, stirring now and then, until a fork slides easily into the potatoes. Then turn the heat to low.",
"timer": 15
}
]
},
{
"title": "Finish",
"steps": [
{
"text": "<b>Melt the cream cheese.</b> Stir in the cubes and let them sit 2–3 minutes.",
"timer": 2
},
{
"text": "<b>Blend about half.</b> Submerge the immersion blender before turning it on, then blend in short bursts for 30–60 seconds, until no streaks remain and about half the potatoes are smooth. Don't blend it fully smooth, or it turns gluey. Turn it off before lifting it out."
},
{
"text": "<b>Adjust.</b> Stir well and taste. Add seasoned salt as needed, or thin with ½ cup broth at a time."
},
{
"text": "<b>Serve.</b> Stir, ladle into bowls, and add toppings."
},
{
"para": true,
"text": "<b>No immersion blender?</b> Blend 3 cups of soup with half the cream cheese in a regular blender (no more than half full, center cap out, towel over the hole), return it to the pot, and repeat. Or mash right in the pot."
}
]
}
],
"notes": [
{
"title": "Three Ways to Make It",
"items": [
{
"t": "p",
"text": "Same ingredients, three methods."
},
{
"t": "li",
"text": "<b>Stovetop:</b> Food for Her Household (this card), about 40 minutes, the quickest without special equipment."
},
{
"t": "li",
"text": "<b>Slow Cooker:</b> <a href=\"#/wait-patiently\">Wait Patiently</a>, 6 hours on high or 10 on low, hands-off."
},
{
"t": "li",
"text": "<b>Instant Pot:</b> <a href=\"#/answer-me-speedily\">Answer Me Speedily</a>, about 50 minutes, mostly hands-off."
}
]
},
{
"title": "Tips",
"items": [
{
"t": "li",
"text": "<b>Cream cheese:</b> Regular or light both work. Skip fat-free; it won't melt smoothly."
},
{
"t": "li",
"text": "<b>Thicker soup:</b> Blend more of the potatoes, stir in a few spoonfuls of instant potato flakes, or add 2 tablespoons cornstarch mixed with 2 tablespoons water while it simmers."
},
{
"t": "li",
"text": "<b>Potatoes:</b> Russets taste most like a baked potato. Red or gold also work."
},
{
"t": "li",
"text": "<b>Bacon:</b> Bake the beef bacon ahead and crumble it on top, saving the grease for the soup. Turkey bacon cooks faster, so cook it separately."
}
]
},
{
"title": "Make Ahead and Storage",
"items": [
{
"t": "li",
"text": "<b>Make ahead:</b> Cook up to 2 days ahead and stir in the cream cheese just before serving."
},
{
"t": "li",
"text": "<b>Fridge:</b> 3–4 days, sealed. Cool it first, and don't leave it out more than 2 hours."
},
{
"t": "li",
"text": "<b>Freezer:</b> Several months. Thaw overnight in the fridge and reheat gently, stirring. A hard boil changes the texture."
}
]
},
{
"title": "Clean-Eating Notes",
"items": [
{
"t": "li",
"text": "<b>Bacon:</b> Beef bacon, beef bacon grease, or turkey bacon only. Never pork, and skip the ham topping the original suggests."
},
{
"t": "li",
"text": "<b>Labels:</b> Check boxed broth, bouillon, and seasoned salt for other meat stocks or flavorings."
},
{
"t": "li",
"text": "<b>Cheese:</b> Some cheeses use animal rennet. Kosher-certified cheese avoids the question."
}
]
},
{
"title": "Feast Suggestions",
"items": [
{
"t": "li",
"text": "<b>Sukkot:</b> Warm soup for cool evenings in the sukkah. See the <a href=\"#/rejoice-seven-days\">Sukkot Feast Menu</a>."
},
{
"t": "li",
"text": "<b>Hanukkah:</b> Potatoes, just like latkes."
},
{
"t": "li",
"text": "<b>Shabbat:</b> Make it before sundown Friday and keep it warm."
}
]
}
]
