"sections": [
{
"title": "",
"steps": [
{
"text": "<b>Spread.</b> Unroll the puff pastry on a sheet of parchment paper. Spread the Divina Chili Fig Spread evenly over the top, leaving about 1 inch or less bare along the edges."
},
{
"text": "<b>Add the toppings.</b> Crumble the goat cheese evenly over the spread. Sprinkle the brown sugar and thyme evenly on top."
},
{
"text": "<b>Roll.</b> Starting from a short side, gently roll the pastry into a tight log so nothing spills out the sides. Wrap the parchment paper around the log."
},
{
"text": "<b>Chill.</b> Freeze the log for 20 minutes so the filling doesn't leak. Meanwhile, preheat the oven to 400°F.",
"timer": 20
},
{
"text": "<b>Slice.</b> Unwrap the log. With a very sharp knife, cut it into ½-inch pinwheels, wiping the knife clean after each cut."
},
{
"text": "<b>Arrange.</b> Lay the pinwheels out evenly on the parchment on a large sheet pan."
},
{
"text": "<b>Egg wash.</b> Beat the egg in a small bowl and lightly brush the tops."
},
{
"text": "<b>Bake.</b> Bake 15–20 minutes, until golden and flaky.",
"timer": 15
},
{
"text": "<b>Garnish.</b> Sprinkle with a little thyme and a pinch of red pepper flakes if you like extra heat. Serve warm."
}
]
}
],
"notes": [
{
"title": "Notes",
"sub": "",
"items": [
{
"t": "li",
"text": "<b>Chili Fig Spread:</b> Sold at Kroger-family stores like <a href=\"https://www.marianos.com/q/cornichon\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Mariano's</a>. We haven't confirmed its ingredients yet, so check the label for gelatin."
},
{
"t": "li",
"text": "<b>Sweet heat:</b> The brown sugar balances the spice, so don't skip it in this version."
},
{
"t": "li",
"text": "<b>Sensitive to heat?</b> Make a separate roll with plain fig spread for a mild option."
},
{
"t": "li",
"text": "<b>Puff pastry:</b> Check the label for lard. Most store brands use butter or vegetable shortening."
},
{
"t": "li",
"text": "<b>Goat cheese:</b> Goats are clean animals (D'varim 14:4). If you'd like to avoid animal rennet, choose a kosher-certified goat cheese."
},
{
"t": "li",
"text": "<b>Make ahead:</b> Roll the log and refrigerate overnight. If it's too soft to slice, freeze 20 minutes, then slice and bake. Or freeze sliced, unbaked pinwheels in a single layer and bake from frozen, adding a couple of minutes."
},
{
"t": "li",
"text": "<b>Leftovers:</b> Best the day they're made. Keep tightly sealed at room temperature or in the fridge up to 2 days, and reheat in a low oven."
},
{
"t": "li",
"text": "<b>Feasts:</b> Sukkot, Shavuot, Yom Teruah, Shabbat, and Hanukkah. Not for Passover / Unleavened Bread (puff pastry is made with wheat flour)."
}
],
"family": false
}
]
